```java
public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
        throws OwnerFieldsMissingException, OwnerTelephoneInvalidException,
        OwnerEmailInvalidException {
    List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
    if (isBlank(request.getFirstName())) { missing.add("firstName"); }
    if (isBlank(request.getLastName())) { missing.add("lastName"); }
    String address = OwnerAddress.normalize(request.getAddress());
    if (address.isEmpty()) { missing.add("address"); }
    if (isBlank(request.getCity())) { missing.add("city"); }
    if (isBlank(request.getTelephone())) { missing.add("telephone"); }
    if (!missing.isEmpty()) { throw new OwnerFieldsMissingException(missing); }
    request.setAddress(address);
    String e164 = OwnerTelephone.toE164(request.getTelephone());
    if (e164 == null) { throw new OwnerTelephoneInvalidException(request.getTelephone()); }
    request.setTelephone(e164);

    String email = request.getEmail();
    if (email != null) {
        if (!EMAIL.matcher(email).matches()) { throw new OwnerEmailInvalidException(email); }
        request.setEmail(email.toLowerCase());
    }
    validated.set(request);
}
```
- `EMAIL = ^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$`. `isBlank` = null or `String.isBlank()`.
- Note: whitespace-only values are treated as blank here (authoritative required-field rule — bean-validation `@Size(min=1)` alone would accept them). Normalized address + E.164 telephone + lower-cased email are written back onto the body and republished through `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` for downstream steps (which read it via `@Val`).

